text:
Here's a simple HTML and JavaScript example to create a colorful website based on your mock-up. This example includes two real jokes:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f0f8ff;
            color: #333;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        h1 {
            color: #4682b4;
        }
        .joke-box {
            border: 2px solid #4682b4;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 20px 0;
            border-radius: 10px;
            background-color: #fff;
        }
        .joke-box h2 {
            color: #4682b4;
        }
        .joke-box p {
            color: #696969;
        }
        .footer {
            margin-top: 20px;
            color: #4682b4;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="joke-box">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <h2>[Really funny joke 1]</h2>
        <p>Why don't scientists trust atoms?</p>
        <p>Because they make up everything!</p>
    </div>
    <div class="joke-box">
        <h2>[Same, but joke 2]</h2>
        <p>Why did the scarecrow win an award?</p>
        <p>Because he was outstanding in his field!</p>
    </div>
    <div class="footer">
        <p>Generated by AI 2023</p>
    </div>

    <script>
        // JavaScript can be added here if needed
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a simple, colorful website with two jokes. You can customize the styles and add more jokes as needed.

Here's a simple HTML and JavaScript example to create an interactive joke website based on your mock-up:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        .container {
            border: 2px solid #333;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #fff;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
            text-align: center;
        }
        h1 {
            color: #333;
        }
        .joke {
            margin: 10px 0;
            font-size: 1.2em;
            color: #555;
        }
        .reveal {
            display: none;
            color: #ff6347;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <div class="joke">
            <p>[Funny Joke]</p>
            <button onclick="revealJoke()">Push to reveal punchline</button>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal" id="punchline">
            Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function revealJoke() {
            document.getElementById('punchline').style.display = 'block';
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a simple webpage with a joke that is revealed when a button is clicked. You can replace the joke text in the `reveal` div with any joke you like. The styling makes it colorful and interactive.
